'' '-s gui' LINKS FOR THE WINDOWS SUBSYSTEM. fbc's option, measured there: no '-s' and
'' '-s console' give PE subsystem 3, '-s gui' gives 2, and fbc hands ld '-subsystem
'' windows'. On the MSVC target the entry point is named too -- lld-link pairs the
'' windows subsystem with WinMainCRTStartup, and FreeBASIC's startup is mainCRTStartup,
'' so a link that got that wrong fails here rather than producing an exe.
''
'' THE SUBSYSTEM VALUE ITSELF IS NOT ASSERTED. The runner can match bytes in a file but
'' not a field at an offset, and '-v' -- which the help says echoes every tool
'' invocation -- echoes none, so the link line cannot be read back either. Measured by
'' hand 2026-09-14 from the PE header: 3 with no '-s', 3 with '-s console', 2 with
'' '-s gui', the same three answers fbc gives.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -s gui -target windows-x86_64 tests/source/plain.bas -o tests/driver/subsysgui.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/subsysgui.exe
